#### 2. Full Code for processChunkRaw (Public & Transactional)
Now that it's public, Spring can override it. We also added Propagation.REQUIRES_NEW so each chunk is a safe, independent unit of work.
```java
@Transactional(propagation = Propagation.REQUIRES_NEW)
public void processChunkRaw(List<JournalBulkValidationService.ExcelRowData> chunk, 
                            String batchId, 
                            String commonRemarks, 
                            String creatorId, 
                            Integer creatorRole, 
                            int globalOffset, 
                            LongAdder globalDebit, 
                            LongAdder globalCredit) {
    
    String sql = "INSERT INTO JOURNAL_REQUEST (REQ_ID, REQ_STATUS, REQ_DATE, CREATOR_ID, CREATOR_ROLE, BATCH_ID, JOURNAL_ID, COMMON_BATCH_REMARKS, PAYLOAD, REQ_BRANCH_CODE, REQ_CURRENCY, REQ_CGL, REQ_AMOUNT, REQ_CSV_DATE, REQ_NARRATION, REQ_PRODUCT) VALUES (JOURNAL_REQUEST_SEQ.nextval, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)";
    Timestamp ts = Timestamp.valueOf(LocalDateTime.now());
    final DateTimeFormatter jsonFmt = DateTimeFormatter.ISO_DATE;
    final BigDecimal SCALE_FACTOR = new BigDecimal("10000");

    try {
        jdbcTemplate.batchUpdate(sql, new org.springframework.jdbc.core.BatchPreparedStatementSetter() {
            @Override
            public void setValues(java.sql.PreparedStatement ps, int i) throws java.sql.SQLException {
                JournalBulkValidationService.ExcelRowData r = chunk.get(i);
                int globalIdx = globalOffset + i + 1;
                String jId = batchId + "-" + globalIdx;
                
                BigDecimal absAmt = (r.amount != null) ? r.amount.abs() : BigDecimal.ZERO;
                boolean isCredit = "Credit".equalsIgnoreCase(r.txnType) || "Cr".equalsIgnoreCase(r.txnType);
                BigDecimal signedAmt = isCredit ? absAmt.negate() : absAmt;

                LocalDate rDate = LocalDate.now();
                if (r.isSystemFormat && r.sysDate != null && r.sysDate.length() == 8) {
                    try { rDate = LocalDate.parse(r.sysDate, DateTimeFormatter.ofPattern("ddMMyyyy")); } 
                    catch (DateTimeParseException ignored) {}
                }

                ps.setString(1, "P");
                ps.setTimestamp(2, ts);
                ps.setString(3, creatorId);
                ps.setInt(4, creatorRole != null ? creatorRole : 0);
                ps.setString(5, batchId);
                ps.setString(6, jId);
                ps.setString(7, commonRemarks);
                ps.setString(8, buildJsonPayloadFast(r, signedAmt, rDate, batchId, jId, commonRemarks, globalIdx, jsonFmt));
                ps.setString(9, r.branch);
                ps.setString(10, r.currency);
                ps.setString(11, r.cgl);
                ps.setBigDecimal(12, signedAmt);
                ps.setDate(13, java.sql.Date.valueOf(rDate));
                ps.setString(14, r.remarks);
                ps.setString(15, r.productCode);
            }

            @Override
            public int getBatchSize() { return chunk.size(); }
        });

        // Precision counting: Only update if the DB transaction succeeds
        for (JournalBulkValidationService.ExcelRowData r : chunk) {
            long scaledValue = r.amount.abs().multiply(SCALE_FACTOR).longValue();
            if ("Credit".equalsIgnoreCase(r.txnType) || "Cr".equalsIgnoreCase(r.txnType)) {
                globalCredit.add(scaledValue);
            } else {
                globalDebit.add(scaledValue);
            }
        }

    } catch (Exception e) {
        log.error("CHUNK_WRITE_FAIL | Offset: {} | Error: {}", globalOffset, e.getMessage());
        throw e; // Triggers rollback for this chunk ONLY
    }
}

```
### Why this is the "Senior Engineer" solution:
 * **Idempotency & Rollback:** By using REQUIRES_NEW, if chunk #10 fails, chunks #1-#9 remain safely in the DB. When the user retries, your DELETE at the start ensures a clean slate.
 * **Observability:** Passing the contextMap to workers ensures your logs always show the batchId, even inside parallel threads.
 * **Proxy Integrity:** Self-injection ensures Spring manages the transactions, preventing partial data corruption that leads to the "Wrong Count" bug.
